      "rrn_counterpart": null,
      "source": "NCBI RefSeq NR_ 16S records, fetched 2026-05-10 by scripts/01b_prepare_extra_mocks.py",
      "truth_kind": "uneven_4_orders",
      "note": "23 bacteria + 3 archaea spanning 10 phyla. Reference 16S is one representative full-length NR_ record per species (no rrn-copy multiplicity). Singer reports DNA-mass abundance spanning 4 orders of magnitude; for taxobench's Jaccard / detection-rate metrics this is fine, but L1/L2 abundance error is not meaningful here (truth is per-species, not per-rep_seq)."
    },
